generated/
src/generated/
pacts/
.DS_Store

# Generated subgraph SDL is checked in deliberately (the gateway composes from
# it and `wgc subgraph check` diffs it); build output is not.
storybook-static/

# Local run output. These capture absolute paths from whichever machine
# produced them, so they are noise in a diff and leak a directory layout.
*.log

# Personal Claude Code settings. `settings.json` is shared configuration and is
# checked in; `settings.local.json` is per-developer and is not.
.claude/settings.local*.json

# Vercel CLI link state, and the OIDC token it downloads alongside it. The
# per-app .gitignore that `vercel link` writes already covers these; this is
# the same rule at the root so a new app cannot miss it.
.vercel
.env.local

# Composed locally and in CI from the subgraph SDL; never committed.
apps/gateway/supergraph.json

# Local compose tweaks. A developer with Postgres already installed needs to
# republish the container on another port, because the host's own daemon binds
# 127.0.0.1:5432 and wins the race for `localhost`. That is a property of one
# machine, not of the project.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Conflict copies from whatever is syncing this directory — `modern.config 2.ts`
# beside `modern.config.ts`, and so on. Three of them reached `main` before this
# rule existed, because `git add -A` does not ask what it is adding.
#
# Ignored rather than merely deleted: they reappear, and a stray `tsconfig 2.json`
# next to the real one is a file somebody will eventually edit and wonder about.
# iCloud conflict copies.
#
# "Desktop & Documents" sync is on and this repository lives under ~/Desktop, so
# iCloud writes a copy named `thing 2.ts` whenever it sees concurrent writes —
# which a build tool touching thousands of files does constantly. 1,531 of them
# were cleared out of this checkout on 2026-08-22, and thirteen copies of real
# source files were once committed to main.
#
# Four patterns, not one. `* [0-9].*` only matches names carrying an extension,
# so it missed directories entirely: `src/routes 2`, `app/api/operator 2` and
# `app/companies/new 2` were all sitting untracked but committable, which is
# exactly how the earlier incident happened. The two-digit forms matter too —
# `oxlint 12` is a real name iCloud produced here.
#
# This is a net, not a cure. The cure is moving the repository off ~/Desktop.
* [0-9]
* [0-9][0-9]
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*
